md=['# Citation Audit Report','',f'Generated: {now}', '', '**Overall verdict: WARN.** All 77 bibliography entries have live existence evidence. The active main article and supplement cite 28 keys in 38 source occurrences; 49 entries are uncited in this scope. Six metadata corrections and one contextual wording correction remain. No entry is classified REPLACE or REMOVE.','', '| Scope | KEEP | FIX | REPLACE | REMOVE |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|',f'| All 77 entries | {counts.get("KEEP",0)} | {counts.get("FIX",0)} | 0 | 0 |',f'| Active 28 entries | {sum(x["verdict"]=="KEEP" for x in active)} | {sum(x["verdict"]=="FIX" for x in active)} | 0 | 0 |','', '## Priority corrections','']
for k in fixes:
    r=next(x for x in ledger if x['key']==k)
    md += [f'### FIX: {k} ({"active" if r["active"] else "uncited"})','',r['note'],'','Recommended: '+r['recommended_action'],'']
    src=r['sources'][-1];md += [f'Evidence: [{src["type"]}]({src["url"]}).','']
md += ['## Scope and execution','', 'Inputs were references.bib and the existing recursive TeX graph rooted at main.tex and supplement.tex. Legacy/historical-note files and previous reviews were excluded. No datasets, RAW files or author contact ledgers were opened. The extracted contexts include file, line and complete surrounding sentences in `.aris/citation-audit/contexts.txt`. The exact input hashes are in the JSON ledger; all were rechecked at completion.','', '**Tooling deviation:** the required `mcp__codex__codex` tool and gpt-5.4 reviewer were unavailable. This run used a fresh collaboration subagent and live primary web/DOI/arXiv/publisher lookups. The exact inherited model/effort and cross-model independence are not certified. No claim is made that the original cross-model workflow ran. Required shared-reference documents were not found by a local filename search; the embedded SKILL.md schema was used.','', 'Each entry has an isolated trace and registry response. The registry batch was retried after rate limits; all 72 DOI records were eventually retrieved. Three arXiv records, the publisher ISBN record for Kay, and the official Codex page cover the five entries without a DOI. Context judgments use the source itself or its publisher/author abstract; source scope was not inferred from titles alone.','', 'The final Chen wording correction uses FIX/CONTEXT because the source remains appropriate: only the manuscript\'s scope attribution needs repair. WARN therefore records a contextual qualification as well as metadata drift.','', '## Uncertainty and resolved apparent discrepancies','', '- Azizi 2023: the accessible primary metadata remains an early-access record. The existing final 2023 volume/pages should not be overwritten with the stale registry values; final primary issue verification remains open.','- Warner 2023: the original paper text supports the moving onset window, V/I trajectories, before-clearing target and load-change false-alarm test. Primary-host PDF access failed; the full-text mirror was checked, without certifying exact byte identity with v1.','- Cover 2006: the publisher confirms the cited second print edition/year despite conflicting electronic-registry year/edition fields.','- Wang 2024: the publisher confirms 121(8):2275–2291; registry volume/issue zero and 1–10 pages are obsolete placeholders.','- Rotnitzky 2000: the author publication list confirms pages 243–284; the registry records only the first page.','- Codex citations identify the disclosed tool. The product page cannot authenticate the authors\' actual usage or historical access date.','', '## Per-entry ledger','', '| Key | Active | Existence | Metadata | Context | Verdict |','|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
